# gitleaks allowlist — this file IS the public CI's baseline.
#
# ⛔ SCOPE: CI (`.github/workflows/ci-public.yml`) runs `gitleaks dir` over the whole tree, and
# dir-mode fingerprints are `file:rule:line` — exactly the form below. So an entry here directly
# suppresses a CI finding, and adding one is a security decision: state what the value is and why
# it is safe to publish. Do not add an entry to silence a real credential — rotate it instead.
#
# (History: the retired private archetype scanned a git-mode *range* with no baseline, whose
# `commit:file:rule:line` fingerprints could never match this file. That scan left with the
# legacy `ci.yml`.)
#
# compose.yaml:173 — STRATA_PROVIDER_KEY for the local `strata` compose profile.
# Base64 decodes to the literal 32-byte phrase "conveyor-dev-provider-key-32byte":
# a hardcoded local default that spells out what it is, not key material.
# Production sealing keys never live in the repo (they come from the SOPS secret).
# Flagged by the generic-api-key rule on entropy alone. (Was :126 until compose.yaml grew;
# re-fingerprint when the line moves — gitleaks dir mode keys on the line number.)
compose.yaml:generic-api-key:173
#
# fixtures/{a,b,c}.flow.json:2 — the fixture id string ("s13.fixture.a" and siblings) in the
# legacy flow definitions read by crates/workflow/tests/trace_expect.rs. Entropy false positive.
fixtures/a.flow.json:generic-api-key:2
fixtures/b.flow.json:generic-api-key:2
fixtures/c.flow.json:generic-api-key:2
